}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-26 20:22] observe — review found count drift across the surface index and registry plus missing routing/governance semantics for many public surfaces.
 >>[2026-03-26 20:24] decide — patch set will preserve the in-flight status cleanup in the surface registry and extend it with launch governance rather than replacing it.
 >>[2026-03-26 20:26] decide — update only the plans most responsible for release gating, QA telemetry, literature traceability, linguistic stability, and contributor formation.
 >>[2026-03-26 20:34] revise — added launch governance, hub segmentation, and explicit backlog/blocked routing semantics to the surface registry.
 >>[2026-03-26 20:36] revise — updated release, DX, telemetry, axis traceability, phase vocabulary, and web-platform curriculum plans to point at ecosystem governance rather than isolated internal craft.
 >>[2026-03-26 20:37] decide — docs/toc should expose the .spw surfaces registry directly so portfolio governance is discoverable from the main documentation map.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:30] observe — independent consumer repositories need a governed installation path: which .spw surfaces ship as dependencies, which are bootstrapped by spw init, and how governance metadata flows into consumer-owned .spw/mount.spw.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:31] decide — the launch ladder should include an explicit "installable" gate between internal-tool and public-beta: a surface is installable when its .spw spec, LSP support, and CLI affordances are coherent enough for a consumer repository to depend on them without pulling the full workbench.
 >>[2026-03-27 09:12] revise — integration model changed to git submodule at .spw/_workbench. "Installable" now means: the surface is engageable through the mount protocol, not publishable as an npm package. The launch ladder gate should test whether a consumer repository can mount the surface via .spw/mount.spw and have it resolve through _workbench.
 >>[2026-03-27 13:16] decide — governance is the canopy, not the bottleneck. Site-install, DX, CLI, editor, and release plans can run in parallel as long as each one names the installable gate and routes readiness claims back through this registry.
 >>[2026-03-27 15:15] decide — governance also needs plan-cluster semantics so execution truth lanes, curricula, discussion/exhibit work, and speculative futures stop competing for one false sense of urgency.
 >>[2026-03-27 15:16] revise — contributor-formation and research lanes stay valued inside governance, but they should feed heuristics and experiments into public surfaces rather than quietly masquerading as release blockers.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:39] decide — add repository-local review to the installable gate: a mounted consumer must be reviewable from its own root without `_workbench` becoming content authority, and the resulting evidence must record both consumer and workbench revisions.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:40] taste — governance should consume review evidence produced by independent consumers, not infer readiness from workbench-internal feature completeness or editor parity.
 >>[2026-07-20 15:15] revise — replace the named-domain portfolio with identity-free surface archetypes; governance now preserves transferable function and stewardship without implying ownership or deployment.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:18] observe — release and install direction still risk collapsing language edition, product schema, runtime protocol, package topology, projection, and consumer evidence into one scalar readiness story.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:19] decide — governance accepts a compatibility/readiness vector and per-claim status; consumer pressure is represented by capability shape and observed evidence, never by a named downstream repository.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:28] revise — Reconciled the five planned commits against git: staging (884d5e87), identity-free abstraction (bca875c7), plan alignment (9c1ebc10, 32859b93, 912eeb0c), and the installable cohorts (40d3e390) landed and moved to done; the verify commit never ran. Remaining: the readiness-vector replacement and a lint verify. Added readiness_reader as the one live question and replaced two vague wonders with a gate audit.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:28] observe — A grep for surface-archetypes across packages, scripts, and extensions finds no code reader; the registry is cited from docs/toc.spw, .spw/workspace.spw, .spw/index.spw, .spw/surfaces/index.spw, a harness eval, and six other plans. governance.status is still the scalar list idea..retired, so the 2026-08-24 per-claim vector has not landed.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:37] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 6 landed, 2 planned, 0 dropped.
}

